  "summary": "I graduated from Northern Kentucky University (NKU) with a double-major. My majors were Communications and Computer Information Technology with a track in Network and System Administration and Security. \n\nWithin the four years, that I attended NKU, I have made an impact on my community with a reach beyond the university campus.\n\nMy contributions to the school over the years include:\n* Programming/Computer Science Tutor through the tutoring center\n* Mentor for the Latino Mentor Program (LAMP)\n* Assistant Associate Member Educator and Co-Recruitment chair of Alpha Psi Lambda\n* Contributed my personal story to aid in the schools' donation campaign webpage \n\nMy achievements and contributions outside of the school include:\n* Ready to Code Educator for the Covington, KY Elementary school district \n* Received a scholarship from the League of United Latin American Citizens (LULAC)\n* Worked as a STEM Mentor for iSPACE GIRLS Camp\n* Participated in Habitat for Humanity ",
